The '''2026 Vancouver municipal election''' will be held on October 17, 2026, on the same day as the [[2026 British Columbia municipal elections|municipal elections]] held throughout British Columbia.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=2026 municipal election |url=https://vancouver.ca/your-government/2026-municipal-election.aspx |access-date=October 1, 2025 |website=[[City of Vancouver]] |language=en}}</ref> Voters will elect the [[mayor of Vancouver]] along with 10 [[Vancouver City Council|city councillors]], 7 [[Vancouver Park Board|park board commissioners]], and 9 [[Vancouver School Board|school board trustees]] through [[Plurality at-large voting|plurality-at-large voting]].<ref name=":0" /> In addition, voters will vote on three capital plan questions and two plebiscite questions related to public safety.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite news |last=Chan |first=Cheryl |date=August 14, 2026 |title=Vancouver council approves ABC's public-safety plebiscite questions for October ballot |url=https://vancouversun.com/news/local-news/vancouver-council-approves-abc-public-safety-plebiscite-questions-october-ballot |access-date=August 18, 2026 |work=[[Vancouver Sun]]}}</ref>

== Background ==
[[Ken Sim]] defeated incumbent mayor [[Kennedy Stewart (Canadian politician)|Kennedy Stewart]] in the [[2022 Vancouver municipal election|2022 mayoral election]].<ref name=":1">{{Cite news |date=November 7, 2022 |title=Ken Sim sworn in as mayor of Vancouver |url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/ken-sim-vancouver-mayor-swearing-in-2022-1.6643066 |access-date=October 2, 2025 |work=[[CBC News]]}}</ref> Sim was elected mayor with 51% of votes cast<ref name=":2">{{Cite news |last=Fumano |first=Dan |date=October 17, 2022 |title=Vancouver Election Results: Ken Sim rolls over Kennedy Stewart, vows to act fast to add police officers |url=https://vancouversun.com/news/local-news/vancouver-election-results-2022 |access-date=October 2, 2025 |work=[[Vancouver Sun]]}}</ref> and was sworn in on November 7, 2022.<ref name=":1" /> The city council, park board, and school board elections, held on the same day, had Sim's [[ABC Vancouver]] winning outright majorities on all three.<ref name=":2" />

